# Allowlist for bin/scan_personal_data.py — tokens judged safe to appear here.
#
# Entries are HASHES, never values: an allowlist of raw personal strings would
# itself be the leak this guard exists to prevent. The scanner prints the hash
# of every finding, so add the one it shows you, with a justification.
#
# Format: <16-hex hash>  # why this is safe
#
# What belongs here: generic English/product words that happen to also be a
# tracker name. The word is not the personal data — the logged ENTRIES are, and
# those live in gitignored data/.
#
# What does NOT belong here: measured values, dates of real events, branded or
# distinctive product names, or anything you'd hesitate to say in public. If a
# finding is real, change the content — do not silence it. Silencing a real
# finding here is indistinguishable from the July 2026 leak that motivated the
# whole guard.
#
# Justifications deliberately describe the token instead of quoting it. Spelled
# out, this file would assemble a list of the owner's actual tracker names —
# an inference the repo does not otherwise offer. To see what a hash refers to,
# run the scanner: it reports the file and line, and the word is visible there.

253d19b8d168c280  # common beverage/behaviour word — journal fixtures + registry category
47320255aceb776a  # generic mineral supplement name — e2e journal fixture
81c6df64b31c9af8  # generic symptom word — journal UI copy + JS fixtures
89d3c95b7b2e4783  # generic vitamin name — e2e fixture + MCP docstring example
c19df0c7bc510763  # generic mineral name — MCP docstring example
d28d5dd75b88e3d9  # generic sports-supplement name — CSS comment
dd8db322cac13ff8  # a shipped coach FEATURE name (protocol banner + toggle), not a log
abb3002e94f17e4b  # generic macronutrient word — fixture name across e2e/trends/MCP/form tests since long before the same word became a tracker (user-ruled coincidence, 2026-08-18)
f833d11cef924479  # generic habit word — journal UI copy + sync fixtures
